  "problem": "$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{10\\text{\u00a0is even}}_{\u23df}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A\u2227B$ is {{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\u2227)$ and \"or\" $(\u2228)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A\u2227B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A\u2228B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{10\\text{\u00a0is even}}_{\u23df}}_{B} & \\,\\,\u2261\\,\\text{true}\u2227\\text{true}\u2261\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
